@startuml Singleton_BotConfigurationManager
' If any modifications are done to the classes participating in this pattern,
' this diagram must be updated accordingly.

title Singleton Pattern — BotConfigurationManager

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FEFECE
  BorderColor #A80036
}

note as N1
  <b>SINGLETON (Creational)</b>
  Ensures one and only one instance of
  BotConfigurationManager exists across
  the application lifetime. Merges
  appsettings.json with NURFLAC_* env vars.
end note

interface IBotConfiguration << Interface >> {
  + BotToken : string
  + AdminIds : IReadOnlyList<long>
  + LocalApiBaseUrl : string?
  + LocalApiPath : string?
  + NginxUrl : string?
  + LedgerDbPath : string
  + UsersDbPath : string
  + HashStrategy : string
  + IsAdmin(telegramId : long) : bool
}

class BotConfigurationManager << Singleton >> {
  - {static} _instance : Lazy<BotConfigurationManager>
  - _config : IConfiguration
  - BotConfigurationManager()
  + {static} Instance : IBotConfiguration <<get>>
  + BotToken : string <<get>>
  + AdminIds : IReadOnlyList<long> <<get>>
  + LocalApiBaseUrl : string? <<get>>
  + LocalApiPath : string? <<get>>
  + NginxUrl : string? <<get>>
  + LedgerDbPath : string <<get>>
  + UsersDbPath : string <<get>>
  + HashStrategy : string <<get>>
  + IsAdmin(telegramId : long) : bool
}

note right of BotConfigurationManager
  Private constructor prevents
  external instantiation.
  Lazy<T> provides thread-safe
  first-access initialisation.
end note

BotConfigurationManager ..|> IBotConfiguration
BotConfigurationManager --> BotConfigurationManager : <<creates self>>\nInstance

@enduml
